      "reworking_status": "discussed",
      "notes": "The authors give one pooled list for very similar miospore assemblages. They report abundant cryptospores from 233 to 123 m, but also place two trilete specimens in the 120–126 m sample. Formations are tentative: cores 9–10 were referred to the Memouniat Formation and cores 1–8 to the Tanezzuft and Akakkus formations; the upper spore-bearing interval is subsequently referred to the basal Tanezzuft. The article also investigates chitinozoans and microphytoplankton. Figure 10 reports Pseudodyadospora sp. separately from the pooled identification P. petasus.",
